                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ethan Meteor Hunter begins as a deceptively easy puzzle-plaformer but the flaws become apparent as it drags on and on. \nIt fails at both aspects of its gameplay: as a puzzle game, there are not enough puzzles (what it's there is decent except those that require twich reaction solutions and get unintuitive after a while), as a platformer, it is repetitive and unfair tier-hard.\n\nI rarely quit games, but this one I just dropped about halfway through the third area, seeking out endeavors that respect my time and don't overstay their welcome.",
